  "type": "MCQ",
  "question": "Consider a rectangular cardboard box of height $3$, breadth $4$ and length $10$ units. There is a lizard in one corner $A$ of the box and an insect in the corner $B$ which is farthest from $A$. The length of the shortest path between the lizard and the insect along the surface of the box is",
  "options": {
    "A": "$\\sqrt{5^2+10^2}$ units",
    "B": "$\\sqrt{7^2+10^2}$ units",
    "C": "$4+\\sqrt{3^2+10^2}$ units",
    "D": "$3+\\sqrt{10^2+4^2}$ units"
  },
  "answer": "B",
